.TH "jeopardy\-questions" "5" "October 5 2026" "jeopardy 0.1.0" "CIC File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
.PP
jeopardy\-questions \(en question set file format for Jeopardy
.SH DESCRIPTION
A question set describes one game: its categories, their clues, and an
optional Final Jeopardy clue.
\f[B]jeopardy\-server\f[R](1) lists the sets found in its games
directory and the host picks one in the lobby.
.PP
A set is a YAML file (\f[I].yaml\f[R] or \f[I].yml\f[R]) or a JSON file
(\f[I].json\f[R]).
The file name without its extension is the name shown to the host, so it
should contain only letters, digits, **_** and \f[B]\-\f[R].
Other names are listed but cannot be started.
.PP
Check a set with \f[B]jeopardy\-validate\f[R](1).
.SH FORMAT
The top level has these keys:
.TP
\f[B]title\f[R]
Name of the game.
Optional.
Default: \f[I]Jeopardy\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]categories\f[R]
List of categories.
Required, and not empty.
.TP
\f[B]final\f[R]
The Final Jeopardy clue.
Optional.
Without it the host cannot start the final round.
.PP
Each category has:
.TP
\f[B]name\f[R]
Column heading.
.TP
\f[B]clues\f[R]
List of clues, lowest value first.
Every category must have the same number of clues.
.PP
Each clue has:
.TP
\f[B]value\f[R]
Dollar value, a positive integer.
Must not decrease down a category.
.TP
\f[B]clue\f[R]
Text shown to everyone.
.TP
\f[B]answer\f[R]
Text shown to the host while the clue is open, and to everyone
afterwards.
Jeopardy style puts it as a question, as in \f[I]What is Mars?\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]daily_double\f[R]
Set to \f[B]true\f[R] to make this a Daily Double.
Optional.
The player who picks it wagers between 5 and their score, or the highest
value on the board if that is larger, and has one chance to answer.
.TP
\f[B]answered\f[R]
Set by the server while a game is played.
Leave it out; a set that has it set is rejected.
.PP
The \f[B]final\f[R] clue has \f[B]category\f[R], \f[B]clue\f[R] and
\f[B]answer\f[R], all text.
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
title: Sample Game
categories:
\- name: Science
  clues:
  \- value: 200
    clue: This planet is known as the Red Planet
    answer: What is Mars?
  \- value: 400
    clue: H2O is the chemical formula for this
    answer: What is water?
    daily_double: true
final:
  category: Space
  clue: The first human in space
  answer: Who is Yuri Gagarin?
.EE
